    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone uniqueness enforcement on `POST /api/owners`, returning **409 Conflict** when a normalized telephone already belongs to another owner.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that reads the validated (normalized) `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Val`, scans existing owners through `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws a checked `OwnerTelephoneInUseException` if any owner shares the same digit-normalized telephone. It normalizes both sides (stripping non-digits) so formatting differences don't create false negatives.\n- `rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneInUseException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- `rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneInUseExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...OwnerTelephoneInUseException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkTelephone` step between `validate` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe check runs **after** `ValidateOwnerFields` normalizes the telephone to 10 digits and **before** `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner`, so a duplicate is rejected before any record is persisted. This follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (functions throw, escalation YAML handlers respond) rather than Spring MVC.",
